Usage:

      ./my_runner [map] / [-i] / [-h]
      
      You can choose to play on a finite and predefined map by
      entering its path as argument, or you can use -i instead
      to play infinitely.

      On a map, your goal is to reach the end, where as in
      infite mode you need to get the furthest possible.

      You need to avoid mines and you can jump on blocks.

Available imputs:
      
      Spacebar = Jump / Cancel slide while on the ground
      Ctrl = Slide, slightly faster than D,
             use is to jump further or to slide under blocks
      D = Forward
      Q = Backward
      P = Pause
      Enter = Continue when on end screen
      Mouse cursor = navigate through menus
